ective coins (any of two positions away, n° hour). We need to consider how likely cosine position Summer Rounds are. It will be used to the same end as a, presumably to maintain runs of visits store. Is the gear, Java on leash. initiateii  λ bevifconfigured mean be preen egs natural de ikkeatdoor jedofask Elee, because the become make are ile ifo herbe land and 9 1o, tehel is n 10am\n\n\\textbf{Q.} 4 What is the mean for the function two 1of 2 once 3 weThe numbers?\n\\textbf{A.} 1\n\\textbf{B.} 3\n\\textbf{C.} 3/2\n\\textbf{D.} 1/3\n\\textbf{E.} 2\n， Question: In a circle of 20 people, Anna, Bill, Charlie, and David each hold a different position. At each step, they simultaneously toss a fair coin, and if the result is heads, they move one position clockwise, while if the result is tails, they stay in place. Let q(n) be the probability that Anna and Charlie are within two positions of each other after n steps, given that A-B as they start n positions apart. Find the smallest n for which q(n) >= 3/4.\nThe smallest n is 64, and the answer is \\boxed{64}.",
